Subject: [PATCH] BlitzInfer: GPU barrier in worker init_device

Wait for the parent gateway to touch ${BLITZ_GPU_GO_FILE} before the
worker makes its first CUDA call. Used by the pipelined swap so the
new EngineCore subprocess can start importing vLLM and parsing config
while the previous engine is still serving on the GPU — the new worker
parks on this barrier until the parent confirms (via nvidia-smi
polling in _wait_for_gpu_baseline) that VRAM has been released.

If BLITZ_GPU_GO_FILE is unset (no gateway, plain `vllm serve` use),
this is a no-op and worker init proceeds normally.

Targets vLLM 0.20.1; should apply with light fuzz to nearby patch
versions. The hunk is in WorkerBase.init_device just before the
torch.accelerator.set_device_index call.

--- a/vllm/v1/worker/gpu_worker.py
+++ b/vllm/v1/worker/gpu_worker.py
@@ -253,6 +253,17 @@
                 )

             self.device = torch.device(f"cuda:{self.local_rank}")
+            # === BlitzInfer: wait for parent go-ahead before first CUDA call ===
+            _blitz_go = os.environ.get('BLITZ_GPU_GO_FILE')
+            if _blitz_go:
+                import time as _t, logging as _l
+                _waiting_logged = False
+                while not os.path.exists(_blitz_go):
+                    if not _waiting_logged:
+                        _l.getLogger(__name__).info('BLITZ: waiting for GPU go-ahead at %s', _blitz_go)
+                        _waiting_logged = True
+                    _t.sleep(0.05)
+            # === end BlitzInfer ===
             torch.accelerator.set_device_index(self.device)

             current_platform.check_if_supports_dtype(self.model_config.dtype)
